==Battleground==
*1 [[Metal Hippoe]] spawns after 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
*2 [[Metal Hippoe]]s spawn after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>, delay 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
*3 [[Metal Hippoe]]s spawn after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>, delay 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Metal Snache]] (10%) spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Metal Snache]]s (200%) spawn, delay 26.67~40 seconds<sup>800f~1,200f</sup>.
**1 [[Super Metal Hippoe]] spawns.
**3 [[Metal Snache]]s (200%) spawn, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
**1 [[THE METAL SLOTH]] spawns.
**3 [[Metal Hippoe]]s spawn, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
**3 [[Metal Snache]]s (200%) spawn, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
**2 [[Pure Gold R.Ost]]s spawn, delay 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage can be beaten easily with [[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Hurricat]] or units with guaranteed [[Critical Hit]]s. If you don't have either, [[Moneko (Special Cat)|Miss Moneko]], [[Space Cat (Rare Cat)|Major Space Cat]], [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Jurassic Cat Sitter]] and [[Cow Cat (Normal Cat)|Lion Cat]] are still enough to beat the stage, but it could take many attempts.

The main problem encountered while playing the stage is the stack of [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal Enemies]]. You'll need fast [[:Category:Area Attack Cats|Area Attackers]] to dispatch those Metal Hippoes and Steel Snakes, and ranged [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|Critical Hitters]] like Major Space Cat or most of the Critical Hit [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Ubers]] to land hits on everything else.

For those looking to farm Lucky Tickets, this stage only gets relatively quick clears with Uber Cannon Start combos such as [[Classic Headwear (Combo)|Classic Headwear]]. If one so
happens to not have any, waiting for a different Lucky Ticket stage to appear is probably a good option.

